{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZEdge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZ4","lean:module:QOU.KZ.FuchsianParam","lean:module:QOU.KZ.Flat2D","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZCorner","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZHexagon"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.edge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.edge","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L261-L333","doc":"**The edge theorem.** Let `N` solve the two-variable system on the square in an edge chart,\nwith unit values. Then there are `δ > 0` and units `c(s)` with `F(s, ε) = N(s, ε) c(s)` on\n`(0, 1) × (0, δ)`, and `c(s) G(s)` is constant for every three-point KZ solution `G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.exists_hasDerivAt_ringInverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.exists_hasDerivAt_ringInverse","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L254-L259","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Ω0_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Ω0_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L251-L252","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.gauge_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.gauge_zero","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L190-L246","doc":"**The gauge step.** If `c` is a unit and, along `(0, δ)`, the `s`-derivative of\n`F = H ε^E` satisfies `∂_s F = Ω_s F + F c⁻¹ c'`, then `c' = −c Ω⁰`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.analyticAt_Ωs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.analyticAt_Ωs","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L183-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.closedBall_subset_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.closedBall_subset_U","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L170-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.commute_Ω0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.commute_Ω0","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L166-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Ωs_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Ωs_zero","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L163-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Ω0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Ω0","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L159-L160","doc":"The three-point KZ connection `Ω⁰(s) = P/s + Q/(s − 1)`, i.e. `Ω_s` on the divisor `ε = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hasDerivAt_F_s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hasDerivAt_F_s","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L146-L153","doc":"**The `s`-derivative along the real square.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hasDerivAt_F_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hasDerivAt_F_e","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L135-L144","doc":"**The `ε`-equation along the real square.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hC","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hMb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hMb","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L129-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hθ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.hθ","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.F","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L123-L124","doc":"The edge solution `F(s, ε) = H(s, ε) ε^E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.H","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L120-L121","doc":"The parametric gauge for the transverse coefficients `M_k = Mt A B k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.smul_cseries_Mx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.smul_cseries_Mx","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L76-L112","doc":"`ε Ω_ε` as a power series in `ε`: its coefficients are `E, M₁(s), M₂(s), …`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.norm_Mt_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.norm_Mt_le","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L62-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.differentiableOn_Mt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.differentiableOn_Mt","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L56-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.ofReal_mem_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.ofReal_mem_U","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L49-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.norm_one_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.norm_one_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L41-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.isOpen_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.isOpen_U","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.U","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L36-L37","doc":"The parameter domain `U = B(1/2, 3/5) ⊃ [0, 1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Mt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZEdge.Mt","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZEdge.lean#L33-L34","doc":"`M_k(s) = −A + (1−s)^k B`, the `ε^k` coefficient of `ε Ω_ε` for `k ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}